<h2>DQ sundaes compared</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Sundae</th><th>Typical price</th><th>Calories</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="/items/strawberry-sundae">Strawberry (medium)</a></td><td>$3.79</td><td>340</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/items/hot-fudge-sundae">Hot fudge (medium)</a></td><td>$3.79</td><td>430</td></tr><tr><td><strong><a href="/items/caramel-sundae">Caramel (medium)</a></strong></td><td>$3.79</td><td>430</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Like caramel? The <a href="/items/turtle-pecan-blizzard">Turtle Pecan Cluster Blizzard</a> mixes caramel with pecans and fudge.</p><p>See every cone, sundae and novelty on the <a href="/categories/classic-treats">classic treats menu</a>.</p><h2>Ways to change it up</h2><ul><li>Ask for half caramel, half hot fudge.</li><li>Add pecans or peanuts for crunch; there is usually a small charge.</li><li>Get a small sundae in the <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> and ask if caramel is an option at your store.</li></ul><h2>Who it is for</h2><p>Caramel fans who find hot fudge too chocolatey. It is the sweetest of the three sundaes, so a medium is plenty.</p><p>All three classic sundaes usually cost the same, so pick the topping you like best. Caramel has the most sugar of the three, so if you want something lighter, the strawberry sundae is the better pick.</p>
